{
  "_README": [
    "Pro forma assumptions for Misty Valley Supply. Every number here is an",
    "ASSUMPTION until Ben replaces it with a real quote, a real invoice, or a",
    "real payroll number. The point of the model is not to predict -- it is to",
    "show which assumptions the business is actually sensitive to.",
    "",
    "Unit basis: one road-legal truckload = ~95,000 linear feet of stud and",
    "track at a blended 0.463 lb/ft across a representative commercial job mix,",
    "against a 44,000 lb road-legal dray limit. See container_model.py.",
    "",
    "Pricing basis: distributor-to-contractor of $0.70-0.95/LF triangulated in",
    "04-unit-economics.md, against verified Louisville retail of $1.268/LF",
    "(Home Depot ProSTUD 25, 3-5/8in x 10ft, checked 2026-09-04).",
    "",
    "Volume basis: 04-unit-economics.md sizes total corridor demand at 40-100",
    "loads/month and realistic new-entrant capture at 0.5-3/month in years 1-2.",
    "The base case ramps inside that range and does not assume otherwise.",
    "",
    "SERVICE PRICING BASIS (revised 2026-09-04 after market research):",
    "The cut/kit premium is capped by the value it creates. Peer-reviewed field",
    "measurement puts saw-trigger time at 13.2 sec/stud and average saw use at",
    "only ~6.2 minutes per worker per day (Schutt et al., Annals of Work",
    "Exposures and Health 68(8), 2024). Full cut-cycle time plus avoided waste",
    "is worth roughly $1.00-1.30/stud; a supplier can sustainably capture a",
    "third to a half of that, which caps the premium at 3-7% of material price.",
    "$0.05/LF against $0.80/LF material is 6.25% -- at the top of that band.",
    "The 30-60% labour savings quoted in the industry belong to PANELIZED",
    "assemblies, not pre-cut loose material. Do not price off those figures.",
    "",
    "WORKING CAPITAL WARNING: base_case assumes 30 days of supplier terms. That is",
    "NOT what a new entity gets by default -- see the no_mill_terms scenario. Mill",
    "credit, earned on Contracting's payment history, is a precondition of the plan,",
    "not a nicety.",
    "",
    "BORROWING BASE WARNING: the OCC's Accounts Receivable and Inventory Financing",
    "handbook notes that commodity raw materials carry the best inventory advance",
    "rates while work-in-process is 'frequently excluded'. CUT-TO-LENGTH, job-specific",
    "bundles look like work-in-process to a lender. Cut to order rather than to stock,",
    "and negotiate the eligibility definition in the loan agreement up front."
  ],
