    "no_mill_terms": {
      "name": "No mill terms -- the credit-application risk",
      "notes": "Identical to base_case except the supplier gives no terms. A brand-new entity normally pays cash or COD until it builds history, and GMS runs 41.5 days of payables precisely because it has decades of mill relationships. Losing 30 days of payables pushes the cash conversion cycle from 80 to 110 days and peak cash from $708k to $1.05m -- the $700k line runs dry. The mitigation is free and must happen BEFORE launch: submit mill credit applications using Misty Valley Contracting's ten-year payment history as the trade reference, and attach the approved limits to the loan package as third-party validation.",
